<article class="env-lemma" id="03TK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03TK">Lemma <span data-tag="03TK">64.11.1</span> <span class="named">(Additivity)</span>.</a>  Let $K\in DF_{\text{perf}}(\Lambda )$ and $f\in \text{End}_{DF}(K)$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Tr}(f|_ K) = \sum \nolimits _{p\in \mathbf{Z}} \text{Tr}(f|_{\text{gr}^ p K}).  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Proposition <a href="/tag/03TI" data-tag="03TI">64.10.2</a>, we may assume we have a bounded complex $P^\bullet $ of filtered finite projectives of $\text{Fil}^ f(\text{Mod}_\Lambda )$ and a map $f^\bullet : P^\bullet \to P^\bullet $ in $\text{Comp}(\text{Fil}^ f(\text{Mod}_\Lambda ))$. So the lemma follows from the following result, which proof is left to the reader. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>